K-SHOT ON LEVELS (unseen ligand), one arm. Columns from most to least contaminated:
  mae_all = every query row; mae_free = condition vector not in the k support rows (same titration
  curve still allowed); mae_series_free = measurement series not in the support either — the transfer
  number. All three are averaged over the SAME draws (those where mae_series_free exists), so the
  gaps between them are real. NULL_kmean = mean of the k measured values, no model — the model must
  beat this, not k=0. n_extractants = extractants contributing to that row.
  none (k=0) = zero-shot over all query rows. none_at_k = the SAME zero-shot prediction
  restricted to that k's masks — compare the calibrated forms against none_at_k, never
  against the k=0 row, which is averaged over a different (larger) set of draws.
